chief: Have you heard what's going on out there?

Harlow: No doubt some sort of monkey trouble and I'm the man to fix it.

Boffin: We don't know where they came from or what they want, but giant apes are attacking the city!

Chief: Normally we'd bring in the army for such a threat but 'round here we do things by the book and the book says that your department handles all monkey attacks.
#You can see why we need you, formalities require your signature to bring in the army. Good, the mayor has arrived. Here, Harlow, fill in these forms.

Boffin: Well actually monkeys are very different to apes...
#Boffin: Well actually the baboon belongs to the monkey family. Apes are...

Harlow: Fool, there's no time. It's my call and I want first shot taking out those hairy bastards.  Of course, to fix this I'm going to need my pilot's licence back.

Chief: Hang on Harlow, if these are in fact not monkeys, the army must handle this.

Harlow: The army's no good here, Chief. it takes a trained professional to fully comprehend the mysterys of the baboon mind.

narrator: Mayor enters...

Chief: At last the mayor is here. Your honor I'd like you to meet Harlow.

